WHILE HTML IS BEING BUILT, PLEASE USE THESE CURL CODES TO CONNECT AND TEST ANYTHING SERVER RELATED:



REGISTER USER:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/auth/register \   
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username":"YOUR USERNAME HERE","email":"YOUR EMAIL HERE","alias":"ANY ALIAS YOU WANT","password":"YOUR PASSWORD HERE"}' \     
  -c cookies.txt



SETUP 2FA:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/auth/2fa/setup \  
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt  

terminal will spit out a gigantic url, copy everything from "data:image:" until a comma (,)

paste the url into a browser, scan the QR code and it should appear as Transcendence in your google authenticator app



CONFIRM 2FA SETUP:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/auth/2fa/confirm \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"token":"GOOGLE AUTHENTICATOR CODE GOES HERE, SHOULD BE 6 DIGITS"}' \                                                                        
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt



LOGIN:


 % curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login \     
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"identifier":"USERNAME GOES HERE","password":"PASSWORD GOES HERE"}' \
  -c cookies.txt

should return a 2FA required error.



VERIFY 2FA:

curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/auth/2fa/verify \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"token":"GOOGLE AUTHENTICATOR CODE GOES HERE"}' \
  -b cookies.txt -c cookies.txt

after this, attempt to curl into dashboard with:

curl http://localhost:3000/dashboard -b cookies.txt

and if credentials are returned, everything is working.

